    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23226" root="شهل" body-key="$">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَهْلٌ</span></b>  <i>A mixture of two colours.</i> (ISk, TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
Hence, (ISk, TA,) one says, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِى فُلَانٍ وَلْعٌ</span> and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَهْلٌ</span>, (ISk, O, K, *) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فى فلان شَهْلٌ</span>, (JK,) (assumed tropical:)  <i>In
such a one is lying.</i> (ISk, JK, O, K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  See also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَهْلَةٌ</span>.

